<% content_for :title, "Pagination" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Components</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Pagination</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">nav</code> of page links, each rendered through
    <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">Ui::ButtonComponent</code>. It's markup only --
    wiring page numbers and hrefs to a paginator (Pagy or otherwise) is host code.
  </p>
</div>

<div id="pagination-preview">
  <%# Preview %>
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted flex justify-center p-8 mb-8">
    <%= render Ui::PaginationComponent.new do |pagination| %>
      <% pagination.with_link(href: "#", aria: { label: "Go to previous page" }) do %>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg>
      <% end %>
      <% pagination.with_link(href: "#") { "1" } %>
      <% pagination.with_link(href: "#", active: true) { "2" } %>
      <% pagination.with_link(href: "#") { "3" } %>
      <% pagination.with_ellipsis %>
      <% pagination.with_link(href: "#") { "10" } %>
      <% pagination.with_link(href: "#", aria: { label: "Go to next page" }) do %>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-8">
    The current page passes <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">active: true</code>, which
    switches its Button to the outline variant and adds <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-current="page"</code>.
    Previous and next are icon-only, so each carries its own <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-label</code>.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#pagination-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="pagination-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_pagination_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Parts %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Parts</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Slot</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">data-slot</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["with_link",     "pagination-link",      "A page link, rendered through Ui::ButtonComponent. active: true marks it as the current page."],
        ["with_ellipsis", "pagination-ellipsis",  "A truncation marker between skipped page numbers. Decorative."],
      ].each do |slot, data_slot, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= slot %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= data_slot %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Notes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Notes</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li>Items render in call order, so previous, the numbered links, any ellipsis markers, and next are exactly the sequence you call them in.</li>
  <li><code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">class:</code> on <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">with_link</code> styles that link's own list item; every other attribute (<code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">href:</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aria:</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data:</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">id:</code>) reaches the nested Button, the part that's actually the link.</li>
  <li>No Pagy (or other paginator) adapter ships here. Compute the page numbers and hrefs yourself and call <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">with_link</code>/<code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">with_ellipsis</code> for each.</li>
</ul>
